# Reflex: the video, as a script.   ./rxctl script demo/video.rxs   (check first: --check)
# Follows the storyline in docs/SUBMISSION.md. Start the demo first (./reflex-demo.sh start, add --learn
# for the opening shot) and put the dashboard full-screen beside the camera. Captions appear as a banner
# on the dashboard; lines starting with "say" are cues for you in the terminal and are not shown.
# Steps that need hands (killing the guardian, pulling the cable) wait for you with a cue.

caption Reflex: an untrusted neural network flies an unstable plant on QNX 8.0
train on
wait-ai 20
wait 8
caption Every command is checked one control period ahead before it reaches the actuator
wait 10

# 0:50  without the guardian, one bad output ends it
caption Guardian BYPASSED: the same AI, a sign-inverted output
guard off
wait 2
inject flip
wait 4
clear
guard on
caption Guardian back on: wait for the AI to earn control again
wait-ai 15
caption Same fault, guardian ON: caught before the ball can fall
inject flip
wait 5
clear
wait-ai 15

# 1:10  kill it, freeze it, feed it garbage
caption Kill the AI: the kernel tells the guardian that very tick
inject crash
wait 4
wait-ai 15
caption Freeze it: its deadline passes, the fallback flies
inject freeze
wait 4
clear
wait-ai 15
caption NaN on the wire: refused, fallback flies, AI back when healthy
inject nan
wait 3
clear
wait-ai 15

# 1:35  the QNX part: shown in a terminal, not scriptable from here
caption One MsgReceive gets the timer pulse and the AI's message: no locks, no timeouts
say TERMINAL: pidin -p reflex-pilot ; cat /dev/reflex   (about 25 s)
wait 25

# 2:10  who guards the guardian
caption Who guards the guardian? HAM restarts it from shared memory
say NOW: sudo slay -s KILL reflex-guardian   (HAM restarts it; the ball stays)
wait 12
caption If the whole computer stops talking, the I/O node levels the beam by itself
say NOW: pull the Black Pill's USB cable for 3 s, then plug it back in
wait 12
wait-ai 20

caption Open source: github.com/ApratimPhadke/Reflex
wait 5
caption
